<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  A real sitemap, which this file was not until now.

  The `_redirects` SPA fallback answers every path with index.html and HTTP 200,
  so before this existed /sitemap.xml returned the homepage's HTML with a 200.
  Google fetched a "sitemap", failed to parse it, and logged the error. Any file
  a crawler is told to look for has to actually be in dist/.

  lastmod is the content date, not a build date: these pages change when the
  product's behaviour or price changes, which is rare and deliberate.
-->
